    skos:definition "A grey, uniform, striated or fibrous sheet but without halo phenomena, and through which the sun is seen only as a diffuse, bright patch or not at all; usually at elevations \\(\\rm{2000–6000 m}\\); vertical velocities of \\(\\rm{0.05–0.1 m s}^{-1}\\)."@en ;
